{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788199544427,"sessionID":"ses_fa7021914ffexcBCZnAM1HV8iX","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_1a1254934ebc427e9bdf70ea","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport inspect\nfrom mcp.server.mcpserver import MCPServer\nprint(inspect.getdoc(MCPServer.run)[:800])\nEOF"},"output":"Run the MCP server. Note this is a synchronous function.\n\nArgs:\n    transport: Transport protocol to use (\"stdio\", \"sse\", or \"streamable-http\")\n    **kwargs: Transport-specific options (see overloads for details)\n","metadata":{"output":"Run the MCP server. Note this is a synchronous function.\n\nArgs:\n    transport: Transport protocol to use (\"stdio\", \"sse\", or \"streamable-http\")\n    **kwargs: Transport-specific options (see overloads for details)\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport inspect\nfrom mcp.server.mcpserver import MCPServer\nprint(inspect.getdoc(MCPServer.run)[:800])\nEOF","time":{"start":1788199544394,"end":1788199544426}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Good. The MCP 2.x API is clear:\n\n```python\nfrom mcp.server.mcpserver import MCPServer\n\nserver = MCPServer(name=\"brazilian-soccer\")\n\n@server.tool()\ndef my_tool(x: int) -> str:\n    return str(x)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    server.run()  # stdio by default probably\n```\n\nLet me check the `run` method signature to see what transports are supported. Also check `run_stdio_async`.\n\nNow let me dig deeper into the data quirks before writing the implementation:\n\n1. Brasileirao_Matches.csv: teams like \"Palmeiras-SP\" (with state suffix), seasons 2012-2022\n2. Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv: teams like \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\", \"América - MG\" (space-hyphen-space separator), seasons 2012-2021\n3. Libertadores_Matches.csv: international teams \"Nacional (URU)\", \"Barcelona-EQU\", seasons 2013-2022 with 'NA'\n4. BR-Football-Dataset.csv: tournaments \"Serie A\", \"Serie B\", \"Serie C\", \"Copa do Brasil\", unaccented team names (\"Sao Paulo\", \"Flamengo\"), dates 2014-2023\n5. novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv: 2003-2019, teams like \"Athletico-PR\" (no space), \"Grêmio\" (accented), \"CSA\"\n6. fifa_data.csv: FIFA players\n\nKey challenges:\n- Team name normalization across files: \"Palmeiras-SP\" vs \"Palmeiras\" vs \"Sao Paulo\" (unaccented) vs \"São Paulo\" — need accent-insensitive matching too.\n- Date parsing: multiple formats.\n\nLet me check a few more data quirks:\n- Copa do Brasil round values (to find \"finals\")\n- Libertadores stage values\n- FIFA data club names for Brazilian clubs\n- Check BR-Football date format and missing values\n\nLet me also check the run() method signature.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_058ffa4e6001NY6jm5H0FqIP24","sessionID":"ses_fa7021914ffexcBCZnAM1HV8iX","messageID":"msg_058ff7459001DRKi5uVpVvv4yF"}}
