th same team-key. But do scores agree? Let me check that quickly in implementation tests. Actually let me just check now.\n\n   Standings correctness check: 2019 Brasileirão champion should be Flamengo (real world). Great validation test. Also 2020 → Flamengo, 2021 → Atlético-MG, 2022 → Palmeiras. And from novo: 2003 → Cruzeiro. Known real champions: 2003 Cruzeiro, 2004 Santos, 2005 Corinthians, 2006 São Paulo, 2007 São Paulo, 2008 São Paulo, 2009 Flamengo, 2010 Fluminense, 2011 Corinthians, 2012 Fluminense, 2013 Cruzeiro, 2014 Cruzeiro, 2015 Corinthians, 2016 Palmeiras, 2017 Corinthians, 2018 Palmeiras, 2019 Flamengo. Excellent test targets.\n\n   Note: 2005 had the whistle scandal with replayed matches (11 jogos do árbitro Edilson Pereira de Carvalho were replayed)... the dataset might have duplicates or the original results. Also some seasons had playoff (2004? no). Let me not hard-assert every season; test a few: 2003 Cruzeiro, 2019 Flamengo, 2022 Palmeiras, 2021 Atlético-MG (from Brasileirao file), 2009 Flamengo.\n\n   Hmm — 2005: Santos vs Corinthians title decided in playoffs? No — 2005 Corinthians won with the replayed matches. Dataset may or may not reflect. Skip 2005 in tests.\n\n   Also relegation: bottom 4 (2006+). In 2003-2005 it was different (2 relegated in 2003? Actually 2003: 2 relegated... complicated). I'll define relegated = bottom 4 for seasons ≥2006, bottom 2 or 4 per known rules? Keep simple: tool reports bottom N (default 4) without claiming historical accuracy; the standings themselves are data-driven.\n\n   Now the FIFA data: club names like \"Grêmio\", \"Atlético Mineiro\", \"Sport Club do Recife\", \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\", \"Ceará Sporting Club\", \"Botafogo\", \"Flamengo\", \"Palmeiras\", \"São Paulo\", \"Corinthians\", \"Santos\", \"Vasco da Gama\", \"Fluminense\", \"Internacional\", \"Cruzeiro\", \"Athletico Paranaense\"? Let me check FIFA Brazilian clubs list — I printed top 15 earlier: Grêmio, Atlético Mineiro, Cruzeiro, Flumin