{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788200465377,"sessionID":"ses_fa7021914ffexcBCZnAM1HV8iX","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_72c5a238bde44495848818c3","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, sys\nsys.path.insert(0, '.')\nfrom soccer_mcp.loaders import parse_date\n\ndef load(fn):\n    with open('data/kaggle/'+fn, encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\nbra = load('Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\nnovo = load('novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\nbrf = load('BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\n\n# Brasileirao: (season, home_base, away_base) -> date\nimport re\ndef base_bra(r): return r['home_team'].split('-')[0].strip().lower()\ndef away_bra(r): return r['away_team'].split('-')[0].strip().lower()\nbra_by = {}\nfor r in bra:\n    bra_by[(r['season'], base_bra(r), away_bra(r))] = r['datetime'][:10]\n\n# novo vs bra date agreement\nagree = dis = 0\nfor r in novo:\n    k = (r['Ano'], r['Equipe_mandante'].split('-')[0].strip().lower(), r['Equipe_visitante'].split('-')[0].strip().lower())\n    if k in bra_by:\n        if bra_by[k] == r['Data'].split('/')[::-1] and False: pass\n        d,m,y = r['Data'].split('/')\n        iso = f\"{y}-{m}-{d}\"\n        if bra_by[k] == iso: agree += 1\n        else: dis += 1\nprint('novo vs bra date:', agree, 'agree /', dis, 'disagree')\n\n# brf vs bra date agreement (Serie A only)\nagree = dis = 0\nmism = []\nfor r in brf:\n    if r['tournament'] != 'Serie A': continue\n    k = (r['date'][:4], r['home'].lower(), r['away'].lower())\n    if k in bra_by:\n        if bra_by[k] == r['date']: agree += 1\n        else: dis += 1; mism.append((k, bra_by[k], r['date']))\nprint('brf vs bra date:', agree, 'agree /', dis, 'disagree')\nfor m in mism[:10]: print(m)\n\n# Brazilian Cup vs BR-Football Copa do Brasil: date overlap & season\ncup = load('Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv')\ncup_by = {}\nfor r in cup:\n    cup_by[(r['home_team'], r['away_team'], r['datetime'][:10])] = r['season']\nboth = miss = 0\nfor r in brf:\n    if r['tournament'] != 'Copa do Brasil': continue\n    # crude name join is hard; count by date only\nprint('cup seasons for 2021-01..2021-04 dates:', sorted(set(r['season'] for r in cup if r['datetime'][:7] in ('2021-01','2021-02','2021-03','2021-04'))))\nprint('brf copa rows in 2021-01..04:', sum(1 for r in brf if r['tournament']=='Copa do Brasil' and r['date'][:7] in ('2021-01','2021-02','2021-03','2021-04')))\nEOF"},"output":"novo vs bra date: 1134 agree / 26 disagree\nbrf vs bra date: 1056 agree / 353 disagree\n(('2022', 'flamengo', 'avai'), '2022-11-13', '2022-11-12')\n(('2022', 'sao paulo', 'internacional'), '2022-11-08', '2022-11-09')\n(('2022', 'flamengo', 'corinthians'), '2022-11-02', '2022-11-03')\n(('2022', 'goias', 'corinthians'), '2022-10-15', '2022-10-29')\n(('2022', 'cuiaba', 'avai'), '2022-10-27', '2022-10-28')\n(('2022', 'corinthians', 'fluminense'), '2022-10-26', '2022-10-27')\n(('2022', 'internacional', 'ceara'), '2022-10-26', '2022-10-27')\n(('2022', 'flamengo', 'santos'), '2022-10-25', '2022-10-26')\n(('2022', 'palmeiras', 'avai'), '2022-10-22', '2022-10-23')\n(('2022', 'sao paulo', 'coritiba'), '2022-10-20', '2022-10-21')\ncup seasons for 2021-01..2021-04 dates: ['2020', '2021']\nbrf copa rows in 2021-01..04: 50\n","metadata":{"output":"novo vs bra date: 1134 agree / 26 disagree\nbrf vs bra date: 1056 agree / 353 disagree\n(('2022', 'flamengo', 'avai'), '2022-11-13', '2022-11-12')\n(('2022', 'sao paulo', 'internacional'), '2022-11-08', '2022-11-09')\n(('2022', 'flamengo', 'corinthians'), '2022-11-02', '2022-11-03')\n(('2022', 'goias', 'corinthians'), '2022-10-15', '2022-10-29')\n(('2022', 'cuiaba', 'avai'), '2022-10-27', '2022-10-28')\n(('2022', 'corinthians', 'fluminense'), '2022-10-26', '2022-10-27')\n(('2022', 'internacional', 'ceara'), '2022-10-26', '2022-10-27')\n(('2022', 'flamengo', 'santos'), '2022-10-25', '2022-10-26')\n(('2022', 'palmeiras', 'avai'), '2022-10-22', '2022-10-23')\n(('2022', 'sao paulo', 'coritiba'), '2022-10-20', '2022-10-21')\ncup seasons for 2021-01..2021-04 dates: ['2020', '2021']\nbrf copa rows in 2021-01..04: 50\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, sys\nsys.path.insert(0, '.')\nfrom soccer_mcp.loaders import parse_date\n\ndef load(fn):\n    with open('data/kaggle/'+fn, encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\nbra = load('Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\nnovo = load('novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\nbrf = load('BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\n\n# Brasileirao: (season, home_base, away_base) -> date\nimport re\ndef base_bra(r): return r['home_team'].split('-')[0].strip().lower()\ndef away_bra(r): return r['away_team'].split('-')[0].strip().lower()\nbra_by = {}\nfor r in bra:\n    bra_by[(r['season'], base_bra(r), away_bra(r))] = r['datetime'][:10]\n\n# novo vs bra date agreement\nagree = dis = 0\nfor r in novo:\n    k = (r['Ano'], r['Equipe_mandante'].split('-')[0].strip().lower(), r['Equipe_visitante'].split('-')[0].strip().lower())\n    if k in bra_by:\n        if bra_by[k] == r['Data'].split('/')[::-1] and False: pass\n        d,m,y = r['Data'].split('/')\n        iso = f\"{y}-{m}-{d}\"\n        if bra_by[k] == iso: agree += 1\n        else: dis += 1\nprint('novo vs bra date:', agree, 'agree /', dis, 'disagree')\n\n# brf vs bra date agreement (Serie A only)\nagree = dis = 0\nmism = []\nfor r in brf:\n    if r['tournament'] != 'Serie A': continue\n    k = (r['date'][:4], r['home'].lower(), r['away'].lower())\n    if k in bra_by:\n        if bra_by[k] == r['date']: agree += 1\n        else: dis += 1; mism.append((k, bra_by[k], r['date']))\nprint('brf vs bra date:', agree, 'agree /', dis, 'disagree')\nfor m in mism[:10]: print(m)\n\n# Brazilian Cup vs BR-Football Copa do Brasil: date overlap & season\ncup = load('Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv')\ncup_by = {}\nfor r in cup:\n    cup_by[(r['home_team'], r['away_team'], r['datetime'][:10])] = r['season']\nboth = miss = 0\nfor r in brf:\n    if r['tournament'] != 'Copa do Brasil': continue\n    # crude name join is hard; count by date only\nprint('cup seasons for 2021-01..2021-04 dates:', sorted(set(r['season'] for r in cup if r['datetime'][:7] in ('2021-01','2021-02','2021-03','2021-04'))))\nprint('brf copa rows in 2021-01..04:', sum(1 for r in brf if r['tournament']=='Copa do Brasil' and r['date'][:7] in ('2021-01','2021-02','2021-03','2021-04')))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788200465367,"end":1788200465375}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait — there's a bug in loaders: `key_of` for stateless names. I look for region entities with same base in registry. But registry.resolve handles this — the stateless merge already merged the RAW NAMES into the region entity. The issue: `canonical_key(\"Grêmio\")` returns (\"gremio\", None), but entity is (\"gremio\", \"RS\"). My key_of fallback finds the most prominent region entity for base \"gremio\" ✓. OK that works.\n\nBut careful — `key_of` with base that has NO region entities (e.g. \"boca juniors\"): returns (\"boca juniors\", None) ✓ entity exists as (base, None) ✓.\n\nHmm, but there's a subtle issue: `canonical_key(\"Atletico Mineiro\")` → alias (\"atletico\",\"MG\") ✓. `canonical_key(\"América FC (Minas Gerais)\")` → collapse → \"america fc minas gerais\" → alias (\"america\",\"MG\") ✓.\n\nAlso the season for BR-Football: `int(when.year)` — I use the date year. That's fine since a Brazilian season spans one calendar year mostly (2020 season ended Feb 2021! The 2020 Copa do Brasil final was played 2021-02-28/03-07 — the Brazilian_Cup file says season 2020 for those. BR-Football rows for those dates would get season 2021 by date year — MISMATCH in dedup key!\n\nCheck: Brazilian_Cup \"Grêmio - RS\" vs \"Palmeiras - SP\" 2020 final on 2021-02-28 (season=2020). BR-Football Copa do Brasil row for same match on 2021-02-28 → my season = 2021 → dedup key differs → DUPLICATE MATCH (same fixture twice, once as 2020 season, once as 2021 season). Hmm! That pollutes \"finals of Copa do Brasil 2021\" with the 2020 final legs.\n\nLet me check how widespread this is: BR-Football Copa do Brasil vs Brazilian_Cup — matches in Jan-Mar that belong to previous season. Copa do Brasil finals are usually Aug-Nov; 2020 was COVID-delayed → final in Feb-Mar 2021. Also Libertadores 2020 final Jan 30 2021 (Palmeiras-Santos) — Libertadores file season=2020; BR-Football doesn't have Libertadores ✓ no clash.\n\nFor Copa do Brasil: Brazilian_Cup (season column) is loaded BEFORE BR-Football. The dedup key mismatch (2020 vs 2021) creates a dup. How many such rows? BR-Football Copa do Brasil matches with date in 2021 Jan-Apr that Brazilian_Cup attributes to season 2020. Let me count empirically and fix.\n\nFix options:\n(a) BR-Football: derive season from DATE but map Jan–Apr dates to previous year? Not generally correct — early-season matches (Feb-May) belong to the SAME year's Copa do Brasil round 1-2. Hmm: Copa do Brasil first rounds are Feb-April (same year), but the PREVIOUS season's delayed final can also fall in Feb-Apr. Ambiguous.\n(b) Match-based dedup ignoring season: key without season? Risky (leagues have same home/away pair across seasons — no wait, key is (competition, home, away) without season — Flamengo vs Fluminense happens EVERY season → would wrongly dedup across seasons! No.\n(c) Dedup with secondary pass: after primary dedup, for rows that produced NEW matches from BR-Football, check if an existing match with same (competition, home, away, date±small) exists under a different season → merge instead. Date-based cross-check: if same competition+home+away+date exists → same fixture regardless of recorded season → merge (keep first's season).\n(d) Simply: dedup key = (competition, home, away, date) when date is not None — but date mismatches across files for same fixture? Earlier I worried about postponed matches. Let me measure: for the overlapping Serie A fixtures (BR-Football vs Brasileirao), do dates agree? Let me check empirically. If dates agree ~always, use date-based dedup primarily and fall back to (season, home, away) when date is None.\n\nLet me test: compare date agreement for shared (season, home, away) fixtures between BR-Football Serie A and Brasileirao_Matches, and between novo and Brasileirao.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0590db33e001hOOjn5VBa2NTt0","sessionID":"ses_fa7021914ffexcBCZnAM1HV8iX","messageID":"msg_0590d338b001Oftl9U1zjbqGo3"}}
