\",\"PR\")... hold on, \"Athletico\" alias in BASE_ALIASES: \"athletico\" → (\"atletico\",\"PR\") ✓. The real 2022 final: Flamengo 1-0 Athletico on 2022-10-29 — Libertadores file has it with season NA, date NA. Is the same match ALSO in the file with real data? The finals list showed 2020 then NA — no 2022 real entry. So it exists only as placeholder ✓ no dup. But secondary dedup: date None → skip secondary check ✓ (needs both dates).\n\nNow implement the secondary pass. Restructure: after primary dict, maintain an index: for quick lookup, map (competition, home_key, away_key) → list of matches (any season). On new row: if a match exists in that list with both dates known and |Δ| ≤ 3 days → merge (fill missing). Else create new. This subsumes... no, primary key still needed for exact same-season dup detection with possibly-None dates (e.g. same fixture recorded once with date and once without → primary key catches via season; secondary wouldn't due to None date).\n\nOrder of checks: primary key (exact season match) → secondary (nearby date). ✓\n\nAlso — those 26 novo-vs-bra date disagreements: primary key catches them (same season+teams) ✓ merged, first (Brasileirao) date kept.\n\nOne more consideration — the ±1-day date mismatches between files for the SAME fixture: which date is right? Trust order: Brasileirao first. Fine.\n\nNow — season for BR-Football via date.year is still wrong-ish for the 2020-final-in-2021 rows, but those merge into the Brazilian_Cup rows (season 2020) via secondary pass, so no duplicate. But what if BR-Football is the ONLY source for a delayed-final fixture? Then season stays 2021 — minor misattribution, acceptable.\n\nWait, actually there's another wrinkle: what about the reverse — Brazilian_Cup 2021 early rounds (Feb-Apr 2021) vs BR-Football rows with date year 2021: primary key matches (season 2021 = 2021) ✓.\n\nLet me now update loaders.py with the secondary dedup. Also note the `import re` unused. Let me rewrite the Phase 3 block.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0590e3bd7001zh8e3U3lQFOzQq","sessionID":"ses_fa7021914ffexcBCZnAM1HV8iX","messageID":"msg_0590db537001ZhoWtkND6GYZu0"}}
