"Inter\" club's Brazilian players got attributed to Internacional-RS. Wrong-ish, but player_count is only used for a summary; the misattribution pollutes team_profile squad info.\n\nFix: add_players should use a STRICTER resolution — exact key match only (no substring). I'll add a `resolve_exact` method: alias + exact parse + base match only (no substring fallback). \"Inter\" → base \"inter\" → no exact entity → no attribution ✓. \"Internacional\" → base \"internacional\" → unique entity RS ✓ +20. \"Grêmio\" → (\"gremio\", None)→ hmm exact: base \"gremio\" stateless → same_base has (\"gremio\",\"RS\") → but that's the stateless-merged entity... after finalize, is there a (\"gremio\", None) entity? No — stateless raw names merged INTO (\"gremio\",\"RS\") entity; the (\"gremio\",None) group was popped. So resolve_exact(\"Grêmio\") → parse (\"gremio\", None) → no region → same_base = [(\"gremio\",\"RS\")] → returns it ✓ (base match, not substring). Good.\n\nAlso display names — fix finalize to set display. And in resolve step 3, same_base includes region-matching. Fine.\n\nOne more: 'bragantino' resolves to RB Bragantino (508) + Bragantino-PA (14) ✓ nice.\n\n'Flamengo' → 1643 + a second with 2 matches (Flamengo-PI ✓).\n\nLet me fix normalize.py: set display in finalize; add resolve_exact; use it in add_players.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0590f61e0001L24fZDiOSF9I9C","sessionID":"ses_fa7021914ffexcBCZnAM1HV8iX","messageID":"msg_0590f1a7e001fGxfEkz9G1GLEA"}}
