ts — again missing matches (3) — Palmeiras matches lost in dedup?! 380-377 = 3 missing. Suspicious: same-pair-same-season appearing twice in BR-Football with different dates >3 days apart (rescheduled matches!). E.g. a match postponed: recorded twice — once at original date, once at played date?? That would be a data error creating 2 rows for 1 match, but my dedup only merges when ≤3 days. If the two rows are months apart → 2 matches → DOUBLE-COUNTED (not lost!). Wait — 377 < 380 means FEWER matches, not more. Hmm.\n\n   Wait actually — let me recount: is 2023 Serie A 380 matches? 20 teams × 38 rounds = 380. BR-Football Serie A 2023 had 379 rows (from earlier count: 'BRF Serie A 2022 matches: 379'). For 2023: let me count raw rows. If BR-Football itself has only 377-380 for 2023, the source is short. And Palmeiras 2023 with fewer matches → fewer points. Real Palmeiras: 70 pts. If they're missing ~2 wins → 64. Hmm but the real issue: why does the DATA lack matches? Let me check BR-Football raw 2023 Serie A count: earlier I printed seasons but not counts. Let me verify: count raw rows for 2023 Serie A, and Palmeiras matches in them.\n\n   Also possible: my dedup wrongly merged distinct 2023 fixtures via the ±3-day secondary pass?? e.g. Palmeiras vs X twice within a week? Impossible in a league.\n\n   Let me check raw vs deduped for 2023.\n\n3. **2021: 418 matches** — 380 expected! 418 > 380 — EXTRA matches! 2021 in both Brasileirao_Matches (380) and BR-Football (Serie A 2021, 380). Overlap should dedup to 380... but I got 418 → 38 matches NOT deduped. Why? Date differences >3 days with same season+teams → PRIMARY key should catch (same season, same teams)! Unless... the team KEYS differ between files! E.g. Brasileirao \"Athletico-PR\" vs BR-Football \"Athletico Paranaense\" — canonical_key: \"athletico paranaense\" → alias → (\"atletico\",\"PR\") ✓ same. \"Atletico Mineiro\" ✓ alias. \"Avai-SC\" vs \"Avai\" → (\"avai\",\"SC\") vs (\"avai\",None)→stateless→(\"avai\",\"SC\") ✓. \"Cuiaba-MT\" vs \"Cuiaba\" ✓. \"America-MG\" vs \"America MG\" ✓ both (\"america\",\"MG\"). \"Red Bull Bragantino-SP\" vs \"Bragantino\"→(\"bragantino\",\"SP\") ✓ hmm.\n\n   38 ≈ one team's worth of fixtures (38 rounds). So ONE team's 38 matches in 2021 didn't dedup! Which team? Probably a team whose name maps differently: \"Sao Paulo-SP\" vs \"Sao Paulo\" ✓ same. \"Sport-PE\" vs \"Sport Recife\"? BR-Football 2021 Serie A team for Sport... wait Sport was in Série B 2021! Hmm.\n\n   Let me find the non-deduped 2021 duplicates: group by (home,away) and count >1.\n\n   Oh wait — 2021: 38 extra could also be Chapecoense/Cuiaba... let me just check empirically.\n\nAlso 2022: 418 — also 38 extra! And 2020: 380 ✓ ok. 2016: 381 (novo 2016 + bra 2016: 380 + the unplayed Chapecoense round-38 match? novo has 381 2016 rows? plausible).\n\nSo 2021 and 2022 each have 38 extra matches = one team's fixtures duplicated. Let me find which.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_059117f28001PEjSWUkJcfWECb","sessionID":"ses_fa7021914ffexcBCZnAM1HV8iX","messageID":"msg_05910faf30010gVGdUDsFahP1E"}}
