sitante'])]\nprint('Botafogo-Flamengo 2009 rows in novo:', len(bf), [(r['Data'], r['Rodada']) for r in bf])\n\nwith open('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv', encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\nn2023 = [r for r in rows if r['tournament']=='Serie A' and r['date'][:4]=='2023']\nprint('BRF Serie A 2023 rows:', len(n2023))\nfrom collections import Counter\nc = Counter()\nfor r in n2023:\n    c[r['home']] += 1; c[r['away']] += 1\nprint('teams != 38:', {k: v for k, v in c.items() if v != 38})\nEOF","time":{"start":1788200815318,"end":1788200815325}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"This is very revealing. Key unmerged pairs within BR-Football itself (the same club in Serie B/C with/without prefix or state):\n\n- \"EC Juventude\" ↔ \"Juventude\" (both in BR-Football! Juventude-RS plays Serie B 2021+; \"EC Juventude\" 2014-2020 era) → SPLIT. Need alias \"ec juventude\" → (\"juventude\",\"RS\").\n- \"Madureira EC\" ↔ \"Madureira RJ\" → split (\"madureira ec\" vs (\"madureira\",\"RJ\")). Alias \"madureira ec\" → (\"madureira\",\"RJ\").\n- \"Floresta EC\" ↔ \"Floresta\" → split. Alias \"floresta ec\" → (\"floresta\", None)?? \"Floresta\" base... CE club. Hmm: entity (\"floresta\", None) exists; \"floresta ec\" is separate. Alias \"floresta ec\" → (\"floresta\", None).\n- \"Cordino EC\" ↔ \"Cordino\": alias → (\"cordino\", None).\n- \"Nova Mutum EC\" ↔ \"Nova Mutum\": alias → (\"nova mutum\", None).\n- \"Tocantinopolis EC\" ↔ \"Tocantinopolis\": alias → (\"tocantinopolis\", None).\n- \"Boavista\" ↔ \"Boavista RJ\": (\"boavista\", None) vs (\"boavista\",\"RJ\") — stateless-merge handles? (\"boavista\",None) stateless → merges into most prominent (\"boavista\",\"RJ\") ✓ automatic. Wait but there's also \"Boavista SC Saquarema\" separate ✓ fine. Actually is (\"boavista\",None) merging into (\"boavista\",\"RJ\")? The stateless-merge rule folds the None group into the most prominent region group ✓. YES handled.\n- \"Campinense Clube\" ↔ \"Campinense\": alias \"campinense clube\" → (\"campinense\", None).\n- \"Moto Clube\" ↔ \"Moto Club de São Luís\": both exist! Same club (Moto Club de São Luís-MA). Alias \"moto clube\" → (\"moto club de sao luis\", None)? Hmm which is more prominent? Both Serie C. I'll alias \"moto clube\" → \"moto club de sao luis\" (fuller name).\n- \"Duque De Caxias RJ\" ↔ \"Duque de Caxias FC\": same club (RJ). Alias \"duque de caxias fc\" → (\"duque de caxias\",\"RJ\").\n- \"SE Gama\" ↔ \"Gama\": alias \"se gama\" → (\"gama\", None).\n- \"Clube Do Remo\" ↔ \"Remo\"/\"Remo PA\": alias \"clube do remo\" → (\"remo\", None)... wait (\"remo\",None) stateless merges into (\"remo\",\"PA\")? There's \"Remo PA\" and \"Remo\" and \"Clube Do Remo\". (\"remo\",None) → merges into (\"remo\",\"PA\") ✓. \"clube do remo\" needs alias → (\"remo\",\"PA\")? If I alias \"clube do remo\" → (\"remo\", None)... the stateless merge happens at REGISTRY level on (base,region) groups — \"clube do remo\" → alias (\"remo\",None) → grouped with \"Remo\" stateless → merged into (\"remo\",\"PA\") ✓ works.\n- \"Sao Jose - POA\" ↔ \"Sao Jose RS\"?: São José de Porto Alegre (RS) — \"Sao Jose - POA\" means Porto Alegre → RS club! vs \"Sao Jose PA\" (Pará) and \"Sao Jose RS\". So \"sao jose poa\" should → (\"sao jose\",\"RS\"). Alias.\n- \"Palmas FR\" — Palmas-TO (FR = ??? \"Palmas FR\" hmm). Leave.\n- \"Villa Nova\" ↔ \"Vila Nova\" — same club!! Villa Nova-MG (Nova Lima). \"Vila Nova\" appears with \"Vila Nova\" stateless and \"Tupi MG\"... wait there's no \"Vila Nova GO\"? Villa Nova is MG. Are \"Vila Nova\" and \"Villa Nova\" the same? Yes — Villa Nova Esporte Clube (MG). Alias \"villa nova\" → (\"vila nova\", None) or vice versa. Both appear in BR-Football Serie C. Merge: alias \"villa nova\" → \"vila nova\".\n- \"Retro FC Brasil\" ↔ \"Retro\": same (RETRO FC Brasil-PE). Alias \"retro fc brasil\" → (\"retro\", None).\n- \"Inter de Limeira\" — distinct (Inter de Limeira-SP, dif