ern ([a-z0-9]) ([a-z0-9])\\b with lookbehind \\b: matches \"s a\" at position... \"as a\": chars a,s,space,a. \\b([a-z0-9]) ([a-z0-9])\\b — try match at 'a' (start): \\b a then need space — next is 's' no. At 's': preceded by 'a' — is there \\b between a and s? No (both word chars). Hmm so \"as a\" doesn't match → stuck with \"as a\".\n\nAlternative: strip dots entirely (no space) when they follow single letters? Simplest robust approach: in collapse, FIRST remove periods: text.replace('.', '') then non-alnum→space. \"A.s.a. - AL\" → \"Asa - AL\" → suffix strip → \"Asa\" → \"asa\" ✓!! \"4 de Julho\" unaffected ✓. \"Operario Ferroviario Esporte C - PR\" — no dots ✓. Any club where removing dots merges words wrongly? \"F.R.C.\"? none in data. Removing dots globally is safe for this data. But careful — \"A.b.c.\" vs \"ABC\": both → \"abc\" ✓ MERGE achieved. \n\nWait but suffix strip happens on the RAW name BEFORE collapse: \"A.b.c. - RN\" → suffix regex strips \" - RN\" ✓ → \"A.b.c.\" → collapse (dots removed) → \"abc\" ✓. And \"ABC - RN\" → \"abc\" ✓. \n\nAlso need alias \"asa al\"? \"ASA AL\" → (\"asa\",\"AL\") ✓ auto-parse. And \"A.s.a. - AL\" → (\"asa\",\"AL\") ✓ merge. But ALSO \"ASA\" stateless → (\"asa\",None) → stateless-merge → AL ✓.\n\nHmm wait — is ASA (AL) the same as \"A.s.a. - AL\"? Yes — Agremiação Sportiva Arapiraquense. ✓\n\nLet me update collapse() to remove periods first. Also check for other dotted names in the Copa file. Let me grep for dots in team names.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05913d508001QP4ZZqD15pPlMY","sessionID":"ses_fa7021914ffexcBCZnAM1HV8iX","messageID":"msg_05913646d001PLQW4FA03I7VIU"}}
