play(k)} {v}\" for k, v in sorted(agg.items()))\n    ranked = sorted(agg.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1])\n    if ranked[0][1] > ranked[1][1]:\n        return f\"Aggregate: {total} — {self._display(ranked[0][0])} wins\"\n    return f\"Aggregate: {total} — level (penalties not in dataset)\"\n```\n\nAnd finals():\n```python\ndef finals(self, competition=None, season=None):\n    comp = self._resolve_competition(competition)\n    year = self._season_of(season)\n    matches = self._select(competition=comp, season=year)\n    finals = [m for m in matches if _is_final(m)]\n    ...\n    groups = {}\n    for m in finals:\n        gk = (m.season, tuple(sorted((m.home, m.away))), m.competition)\n        groups.setdefault(gk, []).append(m)\n    lines = [...]\n    for (season_key, pair, comp_name), ms in sorted(groups.items(), key=lambda kv: (kv[0][0] or 0, kv[0][2])):\n        ms = sorted(ms, key=lambda m: m.date or date.min)\n        ...\n```\n\nAlso `_is_final(m)`: \"final\" in round_label.lower() and \"semi\" not in... round_label \"Final\" ✓, Libertadores stage \"final\" ✓. Careful: \"Quarterfinals\" contains \"final\"!! \"quarterfinals\".contains(\"final\") → TRUE. Damn. Need exact match: round_label.lower() == \"final\" or stage == \"final\". Let me use exact.\n\nAlso in search_matches, `_stage_filter` — the alias handling: \"final\"→ match labels exactly \"final\"; \"quarterfinals\" → labels contain... my filter does `label == wanted or wanted in label`: label \"quarterfinals\", wanted \"quarterfinals\" ✓; label \"final\" with wanted \"final\" ✓; wanted \"final\" and label \"quarterfinals\" — \"final\" in \"quarterfinals\" → TRUE — WRONG for stage=\"final\" search! Fix: exact match after alias mapping, plus allow \"final\" to match only exact \"final\" label. Let me make stage filter exact-match based:\n\n```python\naliases = {\"finals\": \"final\", \"semi final\": \"semifinal\", \"semi-finals\": \"semifinal\", \"semifinals\": \"semifinal\", \"quarter finals\": \"quarterfinals\"}\nwanted = aliases.get(w, w)\nlabels = {fold(round_label), fold(stage)}\nmatch if wanted in labels\n```\n\"final\" in labels: round_label \"Final\"→\"final\" ✓; \"Quarterfinals\"→\"quarterfinals\" ≠ \"final\" ✓ correct. But hmm — Copa do Brasil round_label for round 5/6? \"Round 5\"... user asking \"quarterfinal\" for Copa do Brasil won't match since rounds are numbered. Fine — hint explains.\n\nAlso in `finals()` — the filter `finals = [m for m in matches if \"final\" in fold(m.round_label) or m.stage == \"final\"]` then removing \"semi\" — that wrongly includes \"quarterfinals\". Fix with exact.\n\nAlso `standings` — `row.line()` already includes position. Good.\n\n`_resolve_competition` has a subtle bug: `key.startswith(alias) or alias.startswith(key) and len(key) >= 4` — operator precedence: `or` with `and` — `a or (b and c)` ✓ that's what I want... Actually for key=\"serie a\" and alias \"serie a\" exact dict hit earlier ✓. key=\"brasileirao serie a\" ✓ dict. key=\"libertadores\" ✓ dict. key=\"campeonato brasileiro\" → no alias... startswith checks: \"campeonato brasileiro\".startswith(\"brasileirao\")? No. alias.startswith(key)? No. → None → not found message. Acceptable.\n\nBut wait — the dict COMPETITIONS keys include accented \"série a\" etc. and _fold handles accents ✓. Also \"serie a 2023\"? key.startswith(\"serie a\") → True → \"Brasileirão Série A\" ✓.\n\n`list_teams` uses `self.registry.teams_by_key()` — need to add that method to TeamRegistry:\n\n```python\ndef teams_by_key(self) -> dict[str, Team]:\n    return {t.key: t for t in self._teams.values()}\n```\n\nAlso service `__init__` type annotation `dict[str, sorted set]` is nonsense — remove annotation. Let me fix all these issues. Also `_fold(p.nationality) == 'brazil'` in list_competitions ✓.\n\nOne more: `_select` with venue filter when team None but opponent given — the `elif opponent` branch doesn't respect venue; fine (venue only used with team).\n\n`search_matches` limit: `max(1, min(limit, 50))` ✓.\n\nIn `head_to_head`: `derby = find_derbies(h2h.matches)` — finds matches between classic rivals ✓.\n\n`team_stats` header construction is clunky: `' '.join(label_bits) + ' ' + venue_word + 'record'` → \"Corinthians Brasileirão Série A 2022 home record\" — good enough; `.replace(\"  \", \" \")` handles double space when venue_word empty → \"record\" appended directly: \"all-time record\"? For venue all → \"... 2022 record\". OK.\n\nLet me now apply these fixes to service.py.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0591777780013EHaaKn6XF5NFT","sessionID":"ses_fa7021914ffexcBCZnAM1HV8iX","messageID":"msg_05917019d0015vcANsNIIUewUy"}}
