{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788201297772,"sessionID":"ses_fa7021914ffexcBCZnAM1HV8iX","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_c93687ffcefd4fd4a3deff6b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\nwith open('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\nc = Counter((r['season'], r['home_team'], r['away_team'], r['stage']) for r in rows)\nsame_stage_dups = {k: v for k, v in c.items() if v > 1}\nprint('same-stage dups:', len(same_stage_dups), list(same_stage_dups)[:5])\nwith open('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\nc = Counter((r['season'], r['home_team'], r['away_team'], r['round']) for r in rows)\nprint('cup same-round dups:', {k: v for k, v in c.items() if v > 1})\nEOF"},"output":"same-stage dups: 0 []\ncup same-round dups: {('2019', 'Bragantino - PA', 'Bragantino - PA', '3'): 2}\n","metadata":{"output":"same-stage dups: 0 []\ncup same-round dups: {('2019', 'Bragantino - PA', 'Bragantino - PA', '3'): 2}\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\nwith open('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\nc = Counter((r['season'], r['home_team'], r['away_team'], r['stage']) for r in rows)\nsame_stage_dups = {k: v for k, v in c.items() if v > 1}\nprint('same-stage dups:', len(same_stage_dups), list(same_stage_dups)[:5])\nwith open('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\nc = Counter((r['season'], r['home_team'], r['away_team'], r['round']) for r in rows)\nprint('cup same-round dups:', {k: v for k, v in c.items() if v > 1})\nEOF","time":{"start":1788201297767,"end":1788201297770}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"CRITICAL BUG FOUND! In cup competitions, the same ordered pair (home, away) CAN meet twice in the same season with the SAME venue order: group stage meeting + knockout meeting! E.g. 2013: Atlético-MG hosted São Paulo in group stage (Feb) AND in round of 16 (May). Same (season, home, away) key — my primary dedup key wrongly merges these DISTINCT matches!\n\nI need to include the stage in the dedup key for cup competitions, or better: for cups, only dedup ACROSS FILES. Since raw rows within a single cup file are all distinct matches (the dup examples are within the SAME file — genuinely different matches), cross-file is the only dup source (BR-Football Copa do Brasil vs Brazilian_Cup).\n\nFix strategy: make dedup key include stage/round for cup competitions. But cross-file dedup: Brazilian_Cup round column vs BR-Football (no round info!) — the same Copa do Brasil match from the two files would have different round info (one has round 4, other None). So key with round won't merge them...\n\nBetter approach: two-tier dedup:\n1. Within the SAME source file: dedup only on exact duplicate rows (all fields identical)? No — actually within one file, (season, home, away) duplicates are legit distinct matches (group vs knockout). The REAL duplicates are cross-file.\n2. Cross-file: same fixture from different files. For cups: same (competition, home, away) AND within 3 days AND... stage consistent (if both have stage).\n\nNew dedup design:\n- Primary key: (competition, season, home, away, stage_key) where stage_key = round_label or stage (may be None for BR-Football rows).\n  - Same-file Libertadores dups: different stages → distinct keys ✓ preserved.\n  - Same-file Copa do Brasil: same round number per pairing ✓ (a pair can't meet twice in same round).\n  - Cross-file (Brazilian_Cup round 4 vs BR-Football None): keys differ (round 4 vs None) → NOT merged by primary.\n- Secondary (cross-file): if same (competition, home, away) and dates within 3 days → same fixture → merge. This catches Brazilian_Cup vs BR-Football Copa rows. BUT within-file Libertadores distinct matches are months apart (>3 days) ✓ safe. The 2015 Tigres-River: group Apr 8, final Jul 29 — apart ✓.\n\nBut wait — does the secondary ±3-day pass have cross-file same-file confusion? It merges ANY two matches same competition+pair within 3 days. Within one file, could two distinct matches same pair happen within 3 days? Copa do Brasil 2 legs: swapped venues → different keys ✓. Libertadores: no. Brasileirão: no. Safe.\n\nAlso — with stage in primary key, the previous \"season-shifted 2020 final\" case still works via secondary ✓.\n\nOne more scenario: BR-Football Copa row with date X, Brazilian_Cup same fixture with date X±1 — secondary merges ✓. But BR-Football row loaded LATER (file order) → merged INTO the Brazilian_Cup match ✓.\n\nHowever — what if BR-Football has a Copa match that Brazilian_Cup ALSO has, but their dates differ by >3 days (data error)? Then dup remains. Acceptable risk.\n\nAlso — hmm, one more: within BR-Football Serie A, same (competition, season, home, away) rows can't repeat (league double round robin, ordered pairs unique) ✓. Série B/C same ✓. novo/Brasileirao files: leagues ✓ unique. So adding stage_key to primary only affects cups ✓.\n\nEdge: Libertadores group stage SAME pair same venue order twice? In current format no (home and away legs). 2020 COVID: group stage had some pairs playing both legs same stadium? Even so, different matchdays (weeks apart) — but my primary key (with stage=\"group stage\") would MERGE them if same venue order! Let me check: are there raw dups within Libertadores with SAME stage? From the sample: all dup pairs have different stages. Let me verify no same-stage dups exist... quick check.\n\nAlso Copa do Brasil: same pair same round twice? No (each round one pairing per pair, legs swapped).\n\nLet me check same-stage dups in Libertadores raw data, then implement the fix.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0591a671c001VVa70