stage_key = m.round_label or m.stage` — hmm careful: for Copa do Brasil round_label is \"Round 4\"/\"Semifinal\"/\"Final\"; BR-Football rows have round_label None. For the primary key use `(row.round_label, row.stage)` tuple.\n   - Wait — but for LEAGUES the round_label differs across files for the same match! e.g. Brasileirao \"Round 22\" vs novo \"Round 22\" (same) vs BR-Football None! Serie A match in Brasileirao (Round 22) + BR-Football (None) → keys differ → NOT primary-merged → falls to secondary ±3-day pass → merged if dates within 3 days. We saw 353 date mismatches of ±1 day (within 3 ✓)... but were any >3 days?? Earlier mismatches were ±1 day mostly. Let me think: \"goias vs corinthians 2022-10-15 vs 2022-10-29\" — 14 days apart!! That would NOT merge → duplicate Serie A match! DANGER.\n\n   Hmm wait — that mismatch was on the (season, home, away) join across files — a match recorded at different dates. With round_label in the key, these two rows no longer primary-match (Round 29 vs None) and secondary fails (>3 days) → DUPLICATE.\n\n   Let me reconsider. Better design: stage in key ONLY for cup competitions:\n   - league key: (competition, season, home, away) — cross-file same-season league fixtures always merge ✓ (round labels irrelevant).\n   - cup key: (competition, season, home, away, round_or_stage) — preserves group-vs-knockout distinct matches ✓.\n     Cross-file cup dedup (Brazilian_Cup vs BR-Football Copa) → primary misses (round vs None) → secondary ±3 days catches ✓.\n     But wait — could a BR-Football cup row within 3 days of a DIFFERENT-stage same-pair match wrongly merge? E.g. 2013 Libertadores Atlético-MG vs São Paulo group (Feb 13) & round-of-16 (May 8) — months apart ✓. Copa do Brasil rounds weeks apart ✓. Safe.\n     Also within-file cup \"same pair same round\" (the Bragantino-PA self-match) — drop self-matches anyway.\n\n   What about Libertadores cross-stage matches within 3 days? Impossible (stages weeks apart).\n   \n   One more: cup same pair different stage SAME day? No.\n\n2. Drop self-matches (home_key == away_key) with comment.\n\nAlso — Série B/C from BR-Football only (single file) → league key (season, home, away) — same pair twice per season with swapped venues ✓ unique. Fine.\n\nHmm — one more league edge: postponed league match + replay recorded twice within same file? Would have same key → merged ✓ good.\n\nAnd: what about a league fixture appearing in same file twice with DIFFERENT rounds (data error)? Merged — fine.\n\nImplement now: modify the dedup key computation in loaders:\n\n```python\nis_cup = row.competition not in LEAGUE_COMPETITIONS\nstage_part = (row.round_label, row.stage) if is_cup else ()\ndedup_key = (row.competition, row.season, home_key, away_key, stage_part)\n```\nWait — but `seen` dict keyed with 5-tuple while cross-file league needs exact match on 4 elements ✓ stage_part empty for leagues. For cups same-file distinct stages → distinct ✓; cross-file cup (round 4 vs None) → not merged → secondary ✓.\n\nHmm, but ALSO: cup match in Brazilian_Cup (round 4) + BR-Football (None) — the BR-Football row creates its OWN entry first?? No — file order: Brazilian_Cup loaded BEFORE BR-Football ✓ so Brazilian_Cup rows enter first, BR-Football cup rows hit secondary pass ✓.\n\nBut wait — what about Libertadores stage from Libertadores file vs... only one file has Libertadores ✓ no cross-file.\n\nCopa do Brasil: is the stage/round the same between Brazilian_Cup and BRF rows for the same match? BRF has no round info (None) → no primary match ✓ secondary handles.\n\nEdge — secondary ±3-day for cups could ALSO merge a same-file pair accidentally? Both legs of a cup tie are swapped-venue → different (home,away) ✓. Same-venue-order same-pair within 3 days same file: only the Bragantino self-match (dropped). Safe.\n\nNow also — the earlier issue \"Copa do Brasil 1744 → 1697\": 47 matches were wrongly merged before. After fix: Brazilian_Cup 1,337 raw + BRF Copa 1,123 → cross-file overlap merges → expect ~1,337 + (BRF-only rows). Let me recompute after the fix and sanity check the numbers.\n\nLet me also double check Libertadores after fix: 1,255 - self... no self-matches in Libertadores. Expect 1,255 unique (minus none) → all preserved.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0591b538e001hzfg80cEl7vGva","sessionID":"ses_fa7021914ffexcBCZnAM1HV8iX","messageID":"msg_0591aa9cd001OtjKTYiPMX6ubw"}}
