{"type":"text","timestamp":1788201705019,"sessionID":"ses_fa7021914ffexcBCZnAM1HV8iX","part":{"id":"prt_0592095e8001Xyyv3U04vEcWNM","messageID":"msg_0592022c0001Eg2Yf2aCyzi97t","sessionID":"ses_fa7021914ffexcBCZnAM1HV8iX","type":"text","text":"Found a real bug: `goal_diff` is computed *after* sorting, so ties break on the wrong key. Fixing:","time":{"start":1788201702888,"end":1788201705018}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788201705025,"sessionID":"ses_fa7021914ffexcBCZnAM1HV8iX","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_cca106e265144104bab74485","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-d69f3f5e81d5/soccer_mcp/analytics.py","newString":"    table = sorted(\n        rows.values(),\n        key=lambda r: (\n            -r.points,\n            -r.wins,\n            -(r.goals_for - r.goals_against),\n            -r.goals_for,\n            r.team_display,\n        ),\n    )\n    for i, row in enumerate(table, start=1):\n        row.position = i\n        row.goal_diff = row.goals_for - row.goals_against\n    return table","oldString":"    table = sorted(\n        rows.values(),\n        key=lambda r: (-r.points, -r.wins, -r.goal_diff, -r.goals_for, r.team_display),\n    )\n    for i, row in enumerate(table, start=1):\n        row.position = i\n        row.goal_diff = row.goals_for - row.goals_against\n    return table"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-d69f3f5e81d5/soccer_mcp/analytics.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-d69f3f5e81d5/soccer_mcp/analytics.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-d69f3f5e81d5/soccer_mcp/analytics.py\n@@ -211,9 +211,15 @@\n         away.points += 1\n \n table = sorted(\n     rows.values(),\n-    key=lambda r: (-r.points, -r.wins, -r.goal_diff, -r.goals_for, r.team_display),\n+    key=lambda r: (\n+        -r.points,\n+        -r.wins,\n+        -(r.goals_for - r.goals_against),\n+        -r.goals_for,\n+        r.team_display,\n+    ),\n )\n for i, row in enumerate(table, start=1):\n     row.position = i\n     row.goal_diff = row.goals_for - row.goals_against\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-d69f3f5e81d5/soccer_mcp/analytics.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-d69f3f5e81d5/soccer_mcp/analytics.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-d69f3f5e81d5/soccer_mcp/analytics.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-d69f3f5e81d5/soccer_mcp/analytics.py\n@@ -211,9 +211,15 @@\n         away.points += 1\n \n table = sorted(\n     rows.values(),\n-    key=lambda r: (-r.points, -r.wins, -r.goal_diff, -r.goals_for, r.team_display),\n+    key=lambda r: (\n+        -r.points,\n+        -r.wins,\n+        -(r.goals_for - r.goals_against),\n+        -r.goals_for,\n+        r.team_display,\n+    ),\n )\n for i, row in enumerate(table, start=1):\n     row.position = i\n     row.goal_diff = row.goals_for - row.goals_against\n","additions":7,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"soccer_mcp/analytics.py","time":{"start":1788201705021,"end":1788201705022}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The computed table: Vasco 41 pts (GD -19) vs Fortaleza 41 pts (GD -10). In reality, Fortaleza finished 2020 on 44 points? No wait — real 2020: Fortaleza 16th with 44?? Let me recall the actual 2020 Série A final table:\n\nReal 2020 Série A:\n1. Flamengo 71\n2. Internacional 70\n3. Atlético-MG 68\n...\n12. Coritiba? no...\n\nReal bottom 2020: 17. Vasco 41, 18. Goiás 36? Hmm no. Let me recall properly: 2020 relegated: Coritiba (31), Botafogo (27), Vasco (41), Goiás (37)... and Fortaleza survived with 44? No — Fortaleza 2020: 44 pts is wrong. Actually I remember Fortaleza finished 2020 in 16th? Hmm.\n\nReal 2020 Serie A standings (from memory):\n- 15. Sport 42\n- 16. Fortaleza 44?? no...\n\nHmm, let me look at the computed: Bahia 44 (14th), Sport 42 (15th), Vasco 41 (16th), Fortaleza 41 (17th). In reality: 2020 final: 12. Ceará 49? 13. Atlético-GO? ... The exact real table bottom: 16. Fortaleza 44? I genuinely don't remember precisely.\n\nActually — REAL 2020: Fortaleza finished 16th with 44 points? No — I recall Fortaleza did survive 2020 (they finished 16th)... and Vasco was relegated in 17th with 41 pts. If Fortaleza really had 44, my computed 41 is wrong → data issue in Fortaleza matches?\n\nWait — Vasco and Fortaleza both computed 41 with 10W 11D 17L. Real: Vasco 2020 = 10W 11D 17L = 41 pts ✓ EXACT. Fortaleza 2020 real = 12W 8D 18L? Hmm no...\n\nLet me check: real Fortaleza 2020: 10W 11D 17L?? Both teams with identical records? That seems statistically improbable but possible... Actually I recall the 2020 relegation battle: Vasco and Fortaleza both finished with 41 points! And Vasco was relegated on... no wait — Fortaleza stayed because they had a better head-to-head or goal difference? THE FAMOUS CASE: 2020 — Fortaleza and Vasco both on 41 points; Fortaleza survived due to more wins?? Both had 10 wins...\n\nHmm, actually the real tiebreaker: 2020 Serie A criteria: 1st tiebreak = wins (both 10), then goal difference: Fortaleza GD -10, Vasco GD -19 → Fortaleza above Vasco ✓ MY TABLE SHOWS EXACTLY THIS (Fortaleza 17th above Vasco 16th?? wait no — my table shows Vasco 16th (above), Fortaleza 17th!\n\nMy computed: 16. Vasco 41 (-19), 17. Fortaleza 41 (-10). If sorted by GD, Fortaleza (-10) should be ABOVE Vasco (-19) — 16. Fortaleza, 17. Vasco!\n\nMY STANDINGS SORT BUG? My sort: (-points, -wins, -goal_diff, -goals_for, team_display). Vasco GF 37, Fortaleza GF 34 — both GD... wait Vasco GD -19, Fortaleza GD -10. Sort key for Fortaleza: (41, 10, 10, 34) vs Vasco (41, 10, 19, 37). -goal_diff: Fortaleza -(-10)=10, Vasco -(-19)=19 → Vasco's key is LARGER → Vasco sorts FIRST (better position). BUG!! My sort uses goal_diff ASCENDING-equivalent... I wrote `-r.goal_diff` which for NEGATIVE GD makes the key POSITIVE — larger = better. That's backwards: higher GD should rank higher. For positive GD (e.g. +49), key = -49 (smaller = better) ✓ correct. For negative GD (-10): key = +10 — worse than -19?? NO: -19 → key +19 → sorts BETTER than +10?! WRONG.\n\nThe bug: `-r.goal_diff` only works when comparing... it's plain wrong for negatives. Correct: higher goal_diff should be better → key should be `-r.goal_diff`... wait: sorted ascending by key; want best first; best = highest GD → key = -GD. GD=+49 → -49 (very small, first ✓). GD=-10 → +10; GD=-19 → +19. -10 > -19 so Fortaleza should rank ABOVE Vasco: Fortaleza key +10 < Vasco key +19 ✓ Fortaleza first ✓. WAIT that's correct! -(-10) = 10, -(-19) = 19. 10 < 19 → Fortaleza sorts BEFORE Vasco ✓✓.\n\nBut my output shows Vasco 16th ABOVE Fortaleza 17th. So the sort DIDN'T do that. Why? Points equal 41, wins equal 10, GD: Vasco -19 → key 19; Fortaleza -10 → key 10. 10 < 19 → Fortaleza first. But output shows Vasco first?! Unless... goal_diff is computed AFTER sorting! LOOK: in standings_impl, I compute `row.goal_diff = row.goals_for - row.goals_against` in the loop at the END (`for i, row in enumerate(table...): row.position = i; row.goal_diff = ...`). The SORT happens BEFORE goal_diff is set — during sort, goal_diff is 0 for all rows! So the sort effectively orders by (points, wins, 0, goals_for) → Vasco GF 37 > Fortaleza 34 → Vasco first. BUG CONFIRMED.\n\nFix: compute goal_diff inside the match loop or before sorting. Set goal_diff incrementally with goals. Then real-world check: Fortaleza above Vasco → relegated = Vasco, Goiás, Coritiba, Botafogo ✓ matches reality!\n\nGreat catch by the test. Fix standings: update goal_diff whenever goals change, or simply compute before sort via a key lambda using goals_for - goals_against.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_059209e320018hIIznyV8O6OKq","sessionID":"ses_fa7021914ffexcBCZnAM1HV8iX","messageID":"msg_0592022c0001Eg2Yf2aCyzi97t"}}
